Third-party software

The router daemon (daemon/) is built with these Go modules, each under
its own licence:

  github.com/flynn/noise                  BSD 3-Clause
  github.com/godbus/dbus                  BSD 2-Clause
  github.com/miekg/dns                    BSD 3-Clause
  github.com/vishvananda/netlink, netns   Apache 2.0
  github.com/mdlayher/netlink, genetlink,
    socket                                MIT
  github.com/josharian/native             MIT
  golang.zx2c4.com/wireguard, wgctrl      MIT
  golang.org/x/crypto, net, sync, sys     BSD 3-Clause

PorterKit (ios/PorterKit) uses Apple's CryptoKit on Apple platforms and
swift-crypto (Apache 2.0) where it is built on Linux for tests.


Data

IP geolocation by DB-IP (https://db-ip.com), licensed under CC BY 4.0.
The database is not part of this repository: the image build downloads
it, and the router refreshes it.


The SD card image

An image built by image/build.sh contains Debian and Raspberry Pi
packages, among them the Linux kernel, BlueZ, dnsmasq and nftables (GPL),
hostapd and wpa_supplicant (BSD), and radio firmware under its vendors'
redistribution terms. Those remain under their own licences, which this
repository's licence does not change; whoever distributes an image is
responsible for meeting them.
